    "bodies": [
      "Document 1:\nTitle: Such Great Heights\n\"Such Great Heights\" is a song by American indie pop band The Postal Service.  It was released as the lead single from their debut studio album, \"Give Up\", on January 21, 2003 through Sub Pop Records.  The single includes a previously unreleased track, \"There's Never Enough Time\", and two cover tracks by The Shins and Iron & Wine of \"We Will Become Silhouettes\" and \"Such Great Heights\", respectively.\n\n",
      "Document 2:\nTitle: Iron &amp; Wine\nSamuel \"Sam\" Ervin Beam (born July 26, 1974), better known by his stage and recording name Iron & Wine, is an American singer-songwriter.  He has released five studio albums, several EPs and singles, as well as a few download-only releases, which include a live album (a recording of his 2005 Bonnaroo performance).  He occasionally tours with a full band.\n\n"
    ],
